---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

const updated = '24 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Cookie policy | Radixa Technologies"
  description="What radixa.co.uk stores in your browser, why, and how to change your choice."
  noindex
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <p>
          This page describes exactly what radixa.co.uk stores in your browser. We have kept it
          short because the site itself is deliberately light: it sets nothing at all until you
          choose.
        </p>

        <h2>Strictly necessary</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                <th scope="col">Type</th>
                <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col">Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>radixa-consent</td>
                <td>Local storage</td>
                <td>Remembers whether you accepted or rejected analytics, so we do not ask again on every page.</td>
                <td>Until you clear your browser storage</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          This one is set only once you make a choice, and it is required for the site to respect
          that choice. It cannot be switched off, because switching it off is what it records.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics — optional, off by default</h2>
        <p>
          If you accept analytics, we load Google Analytics 4, which sets cookies in the
          <code>_ga</code> family to distinguish one visitor from another and measure how the site is
          used. IP addresses are truncated before storage. These cookies typically last up to two
          years. Nothing analytics-related loads before you accept — no script, no cookie, no
          network request.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this only to understand which pages are useful and where people give up. We do not
          use it for advertising, and we do not run advertising or social media tracking pixels on
          this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Enquiry forms</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting an enquiry sends your form data to our form delivery provider, which forwards it
          to our inbox. This does not set cookies on your device. What we do with the data is
          described in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Change your choice</h2>
        <p>You can change your mind at any time, right here:</p>
        <div class="btn-group" style="margin-top:20px">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-consent-accept>Accept analytics</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-consent-reject>Reject non-essential</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-status ok" data-consent-msg role="status" style="margin-top:20px"></p>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--grey-500)">
          Current setting: <strong data-consent-current>checking…</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Doing so may mean the
          banner reappears on your next visit.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var label = { granted: 'Analytics accepted', denied: 'Analytics rejected', null: 'Not set — analytics are off' };
      var cur = document.querySelector('[data-consent-current]');
      var msg = document.querySelector('[data-consent-msg]');

      function render() {
        var v = window.radixaConsent ? window.radixaConsent.get() : null;
        if (cur) cur.textContent = label[v] || label.null;
      }

      function choose(v) {
        if (window.radixaConsent) window.radixaConsent.set(v);
        render();
        if (msg) {
          msg.textContent =
            v === 'granted'
              ? 'Thank you — analytics are now enabled for this browser.'
              : 'Analytics are now switched off. Nothing further will be loaded.';
          msg.setAttribute('data-show', 'true');
        }
      }

      document.querySelector('[data-consent-accept]').addEventListener('click', function () { choose('granted'); });
      document.querySelector('[data-consent-reject]').addEventListener('click', function () { choose('denied'); });
      render();
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
